 "difficulty": "Easy",
 "updated": "2026-08-14 09:14:37",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": 1136389,
   "title": "Print Sheet",
   "updated": "2026-07-23 13:14:09",
   "lines": [
    {
     "html": "Reinstall the print sheet.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Make sure there is nothing on the heatbed</strong>. The heatbed must be clean. Any dirt can damage the surface of both the heatbed and the print sheet.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": "caution",
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Attach the sheet by first aligning the rear cutout with the locking pins on the back of the heated bed. </strong>Hold the sheet by the front two corners and slowly lay it down onto the heated bed - <strong>watch your fingers!</strong>",
     "color": "orange",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Keep the <a href=\"http://help.prusa3d.com/article/flexible-steel-sheets-guidepost_2195\">print sheet</a> clean for optimum performance.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "#1 cause of prints detaching from the print surface is a greasy print sheet. <a href=\"http://help.prusa3d.com/article/first-layer-issues_1804\">Use IPA (Isopropyl alcohol) to degrease it</a> if you have touched its surface before.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    }
   ],
   "gallery": [
    {
     "original": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf.jpg",
     "large": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-800x600.jpg",
     "srcset": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-533x400.jpg 533w, https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-800x600.jpg 800w, https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-300x225.jpg 300w, https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-768x576.jpg 768w, https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/1c4bcf6f3f3c0b328a6c52968b72eacf.jpg 1600w"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 1136572,
   "title": "Attaching the stickers",
   "updated": "2026-08-21 12:02:13",
   "lines": [
    {
     "html": "<strong>For this step, prepare:</strong>",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "CORE One+ sticker",
     "color": "orange",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "GEN 2 SN sticker",
     "color": "yellow",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Peel the CORE ONE+ sticker off the base and place it on the CORE ONE+ logo on the door.",
     "color": "green",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Make sure to align the sticker with the outline of the \"ONE\".  Apply pressure and then remove.",
     "color": "blue",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Place the GEN 2 SN sticker above the original SN sticker on the back of the printer.",
     "color": "violet",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    }
   ],
